  "id": "thecodfather",
  "note": "THE CODFATHER — the fishmonger on Filament Street.\n\nThe tile's prose: no glazing at all. The building is a counter with a roof on it: a marble slab the\nfull width of the frontage, canted toward you, open to the street behind a canvas awning on two\npoles, with a crushed-ice bed on the slab and the morning on it in rows. The ice melts off the front\nedge all day. The name is painted blue on white on the fascia, in lettering much older than the man\nbehind the slab.\n\nSo the front is open: a dark interior behind a full-width marble counter with a pale bed of ice on\nit, the canvas awning let down over it, and the white fascia above with the name in blue. The shop\nbehind is white glazed tile and one storey.",
